       "baseline_note": "80 → 81 on 2026-08-03 (release 9.15.0 gate). This RECORDS growth that already shipped through its own reviewed PR; it does not authorize new surface. The +1 is f02db54c2 (fix(cli): register routing:doctor in the CLI registry) — the command existed, only its registry entry was missing, and the registering PR did not move this budget. The gate did its job again: breach WARNS on main and BLOCKS on release, which is the conscious-decision point rather than a silently raised cap. Re-measured 2026-08-03 via the pinned method: 81. Headroom stays zero by design — the next registry addition must move this number in its own PR. 81 → 82 on 2026-08-04: the `handoff` subcommand (road-to-agent-handoff-resume Phase 4) registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Re-measured via the pinned method: 82. 82 → 84 on 2026-08-04: the `route:explain` + `route:audit` verbs (routing-correctness validation surface) register in the same PR that adds the surface. Re-measured via the pinned method: 84. 84 → 85 on 2026-08-05: the `settings:set` verb (road-to-zero-ceremony-settings Phase 2 — the one agent-reachable settings writer) registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Re-measured via the pinned method: 85. 85 → 86 on 2026-08-06: the `conformance:behavior` verb (road-to-agent-behavior-conformance Phase 5 — replays the local transcript store through the four mechanised conformance checks) registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Re-measured via the pinned method: 86. 86 → 88 on 2026-08-07: the `sessions:list` + `sessions:claim` verbs (road-to-parallel-session-coordination — the shell surface of the shared session register, needed because /roadmap:next is command markdown and can only reach the register through a shell call) register in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Re-measured via the pinned method: 88. 88 → 89 on 2026-08-08: the `council:status` verb registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. It exists because an agent in a consumer project announced \"kein Council konfiguriert (keine .agent-settings.yml)\" and substituted a weaker path while the council was configured user-globally the whole time — there was no verb that answered availability, so the only route was an inference from a filename, and the intuitive filename is the one location ADR-104 guarantees is never consulted. Re-measured via the pinned method: 89. 89 → 91 on 2026-08-08: the `self-repair:status` + `self-repair:release` verbs (the queued-defect reader and the single Hard-Floor-gated outward step of the self-repair loop — the loop is deliberately unable to publish unless a human runs the release command) register in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Landed alongside the +1 council:status move in the same branch. Re-measured via the pinned method: 91. 91 → 94 on 2026-08-08: the `packs:active`, `settings:get` and `mcp:available` verbs (road-to-capability-answerability Phase 2 — the three capability probes for the gaps that had none) register in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Each answers a question that was previously only inferable from a filename: which packs are active and from which file, what a setting resolves to and which file set it, and what is declared in mcp.json versus what can actually launch. 94 -> 95 in the same PR: `brand:status` (Phase 2.4 — brand-layer presence, which the rule depended on and no surface could answer). Re-measured twice via the pinned method on the unchanged tree: 95/95. 95 → 96 on 2026-08-10: the `session:recycle` verb (road-to-token-economy-recycling Phase 2.2 — the deterministic producer of the main-session recycle envelope; the recycle advisory names this exact verb, so it must exist as a shell surface) registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Re-measured via the pinned method: 96. 96 -> 97 on 2026-08-10: the `gates` verb registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. It exists because the blocker fields the dashboard already parses (Owner, What to do, Resolved when — CI-enforced by lint_roadmap_blockers) had no owner-filtered reader: the dashboard counts the open blockers across a 600-line file and links each to a per-roadmap anchor, so \"which of these are mine\" was a manual read of every anchor. The same inference-from-a-filename shape as the council:status entry above, one layer up. This branch and the session:recycle branch each measured 96 independently and landed on the same number for different verbs; the merge makes it 97, re-measured twice via the pinned method on the merged tree: 97/97. 97 -> 98 on 2026-08-15: the `workspace:doctor` verb (road-to-inbox-harvest-2026-08-c-workspace-identity Phase 3 — the read-only report over the new `workspaceIdentity()` resolver) registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. It exists for the same inference-from-a-filename shape as the council:status and gates entries above, one layer down: the tree answered \"where am I\" in eight ad-hoc places across six files, and the 12.0.0 span shipped the same worktree misclassification twice, so no verb could be asked which checkout is the main one. Read-only by construction — the roadmap's Non-goals put worktree disposal out of scope and its Risk 3 names \"the pressure read becomes a disposal path by accident\" as the failure to design against, so the command carries no --fix and no --prune. Re-measured twice via the pinned method on the unchanged tree: 98/98. 98 -> 99 on 2026-08-17: the `council:quota` verb (road-to-council-quota-accounting-truth Phase 2) registers in the same PR that adds the surface, per this record's own contract. Exactly the inference-from-a-filename shape as the council:status entry above, one layer down: `cmd_quota` had ex